<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9830" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">concinnātor</span></b> ,
		ōris, m.
		id. (post-Aug.). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>An arranger, disposer</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">capitum et capillorum,</span>”
				<i>a hair-dresser</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
				1</span></i>
			, prooem. § 5. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A maker, contriver, author, inventor</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">causarum,</span>”
				<i>an advocate</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					1, 16, 9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">concinnatores atque inventores tantarum
					deformitatum (poetae),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Arn. 4, 149</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">criminum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 3, 13</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
